text.section:
A corporation shall keep a copy of the following records:

Its articles or restated articles of incorporation, all amendments to them currently in effect, and any notices to members referred to in subdivision L 5 of § 13.1-804 regarding facts on which a filed document is dependent;


Its bylaws or restated bylaws and all amendments to them currently in effect;


Resolutions adopted by its board of directors creating one or more classes of members, and fixing their relative rights, preferences, and limitations;


The minutes of all members' meetings, and records of all action taken by members without a meeting, for the past three years;


All written communications to members generally within the past three years;


A list of the names and business addresses of its current directors and officers; and


Its most recent annual report delivered to the Commission under § 13.1-936.
